# OpenSCAD custom 3D models

This repo is parametric OpenSCAD. A `.scad` file is the model: the script is compiled into a solid, not edited as a mesh. Follow the [OpenSCAD User Manual](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/OpenSCAD_User_Manual) and the [Language Reference](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/OpenSCAD_User_Manual/The_OpenSCAD_Language).

## Parameters

- Write comments, Customizer section names, parameter captions, and `assert()` messages in English.
- OpenSCAD is unitless. Put a header comment that names the unit. Default is millimetres unless that file says otherwise.
- Assign Customizer parameters at top level, before the first `module` or `function`. Group them with `/* [Section] */`. Hide internals with `/* [Hidden] */`.
- No magic numbers in geometry. Name every dimension. Validate ranges with `assert()`.

## Geometry

- Build solids with CSG (`union`, `difference`, `intersection`) and extrusion (`linear_extrude`, `rotate_extrude`) of 2D primitives.
- `module` for reusable parts; `function` for pure calculations. Operator modules take `children()`.
- In `difference()`, the first child is kept and the rest are subtracted. Overlap every cut by a small epsilon so faces are not coincident (CGAL fails or preview flickers on shared faces).
- Curve resolution comes from `$fa` / `$fs`, or one `fn` parameter passed into circles and spheres. Do not set a large global `$fn`.
- Avoid `minkowski()` and `hull()` on already-complex solids; they dominate render time.

## Preview, render, export

- F5 Preview (OpenCSG) is an approximation. F6 Render (CGAL) is the exact mesh. Export STL, 3MF, OFF, or AMF only after a successful F6.
- Remove debug modifiers (`#`, `%`, `*`, `!`) from any file that is meant to be rendered or exported.

## Libraries

- `use <file.scad>` imports modules and functions only. `include <file.scad>` also copies variables into the caller. Prefer `use` for shared libraries.
- A part file must preview on its own. Do not `include` a script that already emits geometry.

```scad
// ❌ BAD — unnamed size, coincident cut, debug modifier left in
difference() {
  cube([20, 20, 10]);
  #cube([10, 20, 10]);
}

// ✅ GOOD — named wall, cut overlaps the kept solid
wall = 2;
eps = 0.01;
difference() {
  cube([20, 20, 10]);
  translate([wall, -eps, wall])
    cube([20 - 2 * wall, 10 + 2 * eps, 10]);
}
```
